   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Inter-agency SOPs (Police, DPP, Courts, Prison) SOP adoption across</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">This indicator measures the extent to which standardized operating procedures (SOPs) governing coordination and workflow among key criminal justice institutions&#x2014;namely Police, the Director of Public Prosecutions (DPP), Courts, and Prisons&#x2014;have been developed, endorsed, and adopted.

Inter-agency SOPs define roles, responsibilities, communication protocols, and processes for case handling, information sharing, transfers (e.g., custody, evidence, case files), and other operational interactions across institutions.

&#x201c;SOP adoption&#x201d; refers to the formal approval and active use of these procedures by the relevant institutions, including dissemination to staff and integration into routine operations.

Progress may be tracked using a staged approach, such as:

stage 1. - Drafted &#x2013; SOPs have been developed but not yet formally approved.
stage 2 - Approved &#x2013; SOPs have been officially endorsed by relevant authorities.
stage 3 - Adopted/Implemented &#x2013; SOPs are in use across institutions, with staff trained and procedures operationalized.</narrative>
    </description>
