    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of South-South symposiums and knowledge-sharing events held on backlog reduction.</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">This indicator measures the total number of South-South cooperation events&#x2014;such as symposiums, workshops, conferences, or peer-learning exchanges&#x2014;conducted to facilitate the sharing of knowledge, experiences, and best practices on reducing case backlogs within the justice sector.

South-South events involve participation from countries of the Global South, promoting mutual learning and collaboration on practical solutions to common challenges, including case management, judicial efficiency, alternative dispute resolution, and digital transformation.

&#x201c;Held&#x201d; refers to events that have been successfully organized and conducted, with participation from relevant stakeholders such as judicial officers, prosecutors, court administrators, policymakers, and technical experts.</narrative>
    </description>
