     <narrative xml:lang="EN">This indicator measures the total number of interoperability assessments that have been conducted and completed within the reporting period. Interoperability assessments evaluate the ability of different information systems, platforms, or institutions to effectively exchange, share, and use data in a coordinated and secure manner.

An assessment is considered &#x201c;completed&#x201d; when it has been carried out using an approved methodology, documented findings are produced, and recommendations are validated and shared with relevant stakeholders. These assessments may cover technical, legal, organizational, and procedural aspects of interoperability across systems within the justice sector or between related institutions.</narrative>
