     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of policy documents on diversion and mediation finalized (Saint Kitts and Nevis)</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">This indicator measures the total number of policy documents related to diversion and mediation that have been formally finalized in Saint Kitts and Nevis within the reporting period. These policy documents may include national policies, strategies, guidelines, frameworks, or standard operating procedures that promote the use of diversion and mediation as alternatives to formal judicial proceedings.

&#x201c;Finalized&#x201d; refers to policy documents that have completed the full development process, including drafting, stakeholder consultations, validation, and official approval or endorsement by the relevant authorities.

Diversion policies typically aim to redirect appropriate cases&#x2014;particularly minor or non-violent offenses&#x2014;away from the formal justice system, while mediation policies support alternative dispute resolution mechanisms that facilitate negotiated settlements between parties.</narrative>
