    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Status of the establishment of Attorney General (AG) roundtable (1. Initiated, 2. Convened, 3. Formalised</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">This indicator tracks the progress made toward establishing an Attorney General (AG) Roundtable as a formal platform for coordination, dialogue, and collaboration among key justice sector stakeholders. The roundtable is intended to facilitate high-level engagement on legal reforms, policy alignment, and strategic issues affecting the justice system.

Progress is measured using a three-stage categorical scale:

Stage 1 - Initiated &#x2013; Preliminary steps have been taken to establish the roundtable, such as stakeholder consultations, concept development, or initial planning.
Stage 2 - Convened &#x2013; The roundtable has held at least one formal meeting with participation from relevant stakeholders.
Stage 3 - Formalised &#x2013; The roundtable has been institutionalized through defined terms of reference, regular meeting schedules, and recognized governance or coordination structures.</narrative>
    </description>
